  "promptEn": "Blues in G. Which scale sounds in the fragment?",
  "explanationEs": "La respuesta correcta es «Escala de blues». En Sol la escala de blues es Sol, Si♭, Do, Re♭, Re, Fa y Sol. Contiene la séptima menor (Fa) y la tercera menor (Si♭), que la acercan al acorde de Sol7. La quinta disminuida Re♭ es la nota azul central y puede resolver a Do o Re.",
  "explanationEn": "The correct answer is “Blues scale”. In G the blues scale is G, Bb, C, Db, D, F and G. It contains the minor seventh (F) and the minor third (Bb), which bring it close to a G7 chord. The diminished fifth Db is the central blue note and can resolve to C or D.",
